## Before you apply

Most institutes publish a **guidebook** (a prospectus) that you can read before deciding to apply
— no login required. Not every institute has one; if there's no guidebook link, that institute
simply hasn't published one, it's not a broken link.

## Starting an application

1. Log in or verify via the code (OTP) sent to you.
2. Your application dashboard shows your current status and a document checklist.
3. Fill in the application form and submit the required documents.

## Understanding your application status

Your application will be in one of these states:

- **Draft** — you can still edit it; nothing has been submitted yet.
- **Locked** — the application has been submitted and can no longer be edited from your side.
  You'll see a locked view instead of the form.
- **Submitted** — locked and now with the institute for review.

If your application suddenly appears locked and you can't make a change you need to, that's
expected once you've submitted — contact the school's admissions office directly to request a
correction rather than looking for an edit option that no longer exists for you.

## Paying application fees

Once your application reaches the payment step, see
[Paying Your Application Fee](/docs/admissions-payment) for how that works and how to confirm it
went through.
